# llm-guard.baseline — exceptions for scripts/llm-guard.py, each VERIFIED BY HAND.
#
# Format:  <doc>  TAB  <key>  TAB  <why this finding is not a defect>
#   key = <cited-path>:<lo>-<hi>   for a `citations` finding
#         symbol:<name>            for a `symbols` finding whose name belongs to another repo
#
# Only `citations` and cross-repo `symbols` findings can be listed here. `paths`, `forbidden`,
# `phantom`, `version`, out-of-bounds and `vacuous` are deterministic and always fail.
#
# The key carries the CITED coordinates (or the symbol name) on purpose: a citation that later
# drifts to a different line stops matching its entry and the gate fires. It deliberately does
# NOT carry the doc-side line number, so editing prose above a citation does not re-key it.
# An entry matching nothing is reported as `baseline-stale` and FAILS, so this file cannot rot
# into a blanket exemption.  Re-derive with: python3 scripts/llm-guard.py --no-baseline
#
# A note's coordinates are of two kinds. One that says where something IS is a coordinate of the
# HEAD, and the superproject's citation sweep moves it with the lines, as it moves the key. One that
# says where something WAS -- a RE-KEYED history -- is written `L<n>`, beside the commit it was read at
# unless its sentence names the change it belongs to: written `:<n>`, the next sweep rewrites it into a
# state it never described (Huly QB-1198).
#
# KNOWN LIMIT, stated because it has already cost something.  A key pins the citation against
# the CITATION moving; it does not pin it against the SOURCE moving underneath a citation that
# stays put.  Rule 2b (the digest) is what covers that — and it cannot key a citation whose
# basename is ambiguous inside this repo, which is 8 of qb's 77 resolvable cited ranges.
# `llm/qb.llm.md` cited `listener.h` L936-942 for the run/run_once/run_until logic_error; the
# throw had moved to L989 and the cited lines had become an unrelated comment about
# thread_local symbol tables, while the entry here still asserted ":940" and absorbed the
# finding.  Corrected to L980-993 when the docs moved into this repo.  When re-verifying an
# entry, read the cited lines — do not trust the note.

llm/qb.llm.md	ssl/context.h:157-157	correct: `class QB_API Context` is qb/src/qb/io/tcp/ssl/context.h:157. `SSL_CTX_free` is named in passing as the thing you must NOT call. RE-KEYED from L127 by the formatting sweep, which added one line above the class, then from L128 by Huly QB-83, which declared `OcspContext` above it; the declaration was re-read at the new coordinate each time, not offset.
